From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikhail Malyshev <mike.malyshev@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 16:10:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] ui/dbus: do not abort the machine on a scanout with no
 texture

dbus_scanout_texture() asserts on tex_id, so a zero one takes down the
whole VM:

  qemu-system-x86_64: Failed to call update: The connection is closed
  qemu-system-x86_64: Failed to call update: The connection is closed
  Assertion failed: tex_id (ui/dbus-listener.c: dbus_scanout_texture: 450)

Observed with a Windows guest on virtio-vga-gl whose display powered off
after an idle timeout, against a D-Bus display client that had gone away
earlier - the listener is only unregistered from dispose, so it keeps
being called after its peer disconnects, and the first scanout without a
texture is fatal.

A missing texture is a frame we cannot show, not a state the machine
cannot continue from. Report it and skip the frame.

The listener outliving its connection is a separate problem and is left
alone here.

Rebased onto QEMU 11.1.2. Still needed there: upstream master keeps the
assert, and it was reproduced on 11.1.2 by updating viogpudo in a Windows
11 guest.

Signed-off-by: Mikhail Malyshev <mike.malyshev@gmail.com>
---
 ui/dbus-listener.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ui/dbus-listener.c b/ui/dbus-listener.c
index 2e2f6ba41..dc7ad0992 100644
--- a/ui/dbus-listener.c
+++ b/ui/dbus-listener.c
@@ -597,7 +597,15 @@ static void dbus_scanout_texture(DisplayChangeListener *dcl,
     uint32_t offset[DMABUF_MAX_PLANES], stride[DMABUF_MAX_PLANES], fourcc;
     uint64_t modifier;
 
-    assert(tex_id);
+    if (!tex_id) {
+        /*
+         * virgl has no texture for this scanout: the guest released it
+         * (a driver reinstall or a display powered off). Not a reason to
+         * abort a running machine - skip the frame and keep the guest alive.
+         */
+        error_report("%s: no texture for scanout, skipping", __func__);
+        return;
+    }
     if (!egl_dmabuf_export_texture(tex_id, fd, (EGLint *)offset, (EGLint *)stride,
                                    (EGLint *)&fourcc, &num_planes, &modifier)) {
         error_report("%s: failed to export dmabuf for texture", __func__);
